---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Field note · Krigsvold baseline"><header slot="hero" class="page-masthead page-masthead--plain"><div class="page-masthead__veil"></div><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-lg-9"><p class="eyebrow text-white">Field notes</p><h1>A longer observation record</h1><p class="page-masthead__subtitle">The page masthead uses a navy photographic-era composition above a light editorial region.</p></div></div></div></header>
<div class="page-shell"><div class="container"><div class="row"><article class="col-xl-8 col-lg-9 editorial-content">
<p class="review-note">Fictional research · Illustrative data</p><p>Representative material exercises the original Krigsvold text hierarchy, margins, link styling, and reading measure.</p><h2 id="questions">Questions and context</h2><p>A long paragraph remains useful for observing line length and the separation between textual and structural elements. The information is synthetic, but the layout follows the actual source.</p><blockquote><p>Clear records are easier to interpret when the hierarchy is visible.</p></blockquote><h3>What the sample establishes</h3><ul><li>Typographic roles</li><li>Section spacing</li><li>Link, focus, and list behavior</li></ul>
<h2 id="data">Measurements</h2><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Station</th><th scope="col">Reading</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">North</th><td>12.4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">South</th><td>10.8</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2 id="controls">Interface controls</h2><form onsubmit="return false"><label for="reference-query">Reference label</label><input id="reference-query" class="site-search-input" placeholder="Enter a label"/><button class="btn btn-dark-blue" type="button">Review</button></form>
</article></div></div></div></BaseLayout>
